{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"JLSEC-2026-1431","published":"2026-11-23T20:01:46.351Z","modified":"2026-11-23T20:15:04.595326434Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-53799","EUVD-2026-58037"],"details":"rsync before 3.5.0 contains a symlink race condition vulnerability that allows local attackers to cause rsync to apply arbitrary ACLs or extended attributes to unintended files by substituting a symlink at a predictable destination path between the file write and the subsequent `acl_set_file()` or lsetxattr() call. Attackers can exploit this timing window to redirect ACL and xattr application through a crafted symlink to files outside the intended destination tree, potentially granting elevated permissions and enabling local privilege escalation.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsync_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/rsync_jll?uuid=191d6b87-264a-55f5-a0e2-c8fbce9a1ce0"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.5.0+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1431.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/releases/tag/v3.5.0"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/security/advisories/GHSA-phxh-hjqv-39c9"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rsync-symlink-race-condition-via-acl-xattr-application"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"affected":{"samba:rsync":["< 3.5.0"]},"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53799","id":"CVE-2026-53799","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:04.996Z","modified":"2026-10-24T16:10:00.153Z","published":"2026-08-13T15:19:52.130Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-53799"},{"html_url":"https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-58037","id":"EUVD-2026-58037","imported":"2026-11-21T02:56:06.498Z","modified":"2026-08-14T18:09:48Z","published":"2026